                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5e572e03-d316-49e3-8b95-e8b5a1914512",
                        "entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "синеку́рах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d96d201e-7d72-31f7-9ec1-3ff48346f8db",
                        "entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. в средневековой Европе церковная должность, приносившая доход, но не связанная для получившего её с какими-либо обязанностями или хотя бы с необходимостью находиться в месте служения"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e924e32-b773-3245-809e-950d2101e69b",
                        "entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., книжн. должность, дающая хороший доход, но не требующая труда"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b3a4afc-0fab-450b-9766-ab38d383b855",
                                "sense_id": "3e924e32-b773-3245-809e-950d2101e69b",
                                "text": "У него был тщательно подобранный штат чиновников особых поручений, и должность эта при нём не была синекура, так как он им давал постоянно серьёзные командировки и всё нужное узнавал через них."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c527247-1543-4cad-8c1f-5c5c7f6e897b",
                                "sense_id": "3e924e32-b773-3245-809e-950d2101e69b",
                                "text": "Заметьте, этот властолюбец ничего не желает лично для себя: он раздаёт огромные синекуры друзьям, а сам беден, как церковная крыса."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "341680fc-f2ab-4a06-8058-85c3fb92c513",
                                "sense_id": "3e924e32-b773-3245-809e-950d2101e69b",
                                "text": "Это была чистейшей воды синекура: юноша этот абсолютно ничего не делал, но он часто напоминал другим, что он брат «личного секретаря», и через свою сестру пользовался тоже известным влиянием на Иоффе."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a9c61e6-ed9c-3851-8e78-194781507370",
                        "entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., устар. место, положение, обеспечивающее беззаботное существование"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e50c0a1-fec7-4e7d-9ea9-cab5d9f6aeff",
                                "sense_id": "3a9c61e6-ed9c-3851-8e78-194781507370",
                                "text": "Она была неутомительна в исправлении визитов: лошади её не пользовались синекурою, а зарабатывали свой овёс в труде и поте."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6c1b3083-21ed-4e53-810e-2a020f6bef85",
                        "source_entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "target_lang_word": "sinecure",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sinecure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                        "entry_id": "5f03727e-c911-33ca-9e75-1fbc2979df72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A position that requires little to no work, or easy work, but still gives an ample payment; a cushy job."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01cffd1e-cc11-4b16-a577-70a0cc5ba074",
                                                "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                                "text": "Miss Briggs was not formally dismissed, but her place as companion was a sinecure and a derision […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c91317b-34c5-413a-b712-29daf57834e9",
                                                "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                                "text": "A lucrative sinecure in the Excise was bestowed on Ferguson."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5a0cb07-5c30-4529-9d53-2df895a323a1",
                                                "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                                "text": "His prospects consisted of a hope that if he kept up appearances somebody would do something for him. The something appeared vaguely to his imagination as a private secretaryship or a sinecure of some sort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d49d2454-8153-4d0c-8f87-5f5609c250aa",
                                                "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                                "text": "With extra traffic, numerous boat trains to and from Southampton Docks, and working of empty stock, his job, like that of most signalmen, is no sinecure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e879be6f-8500-4b90-8b9a-6c3ffb20bcd8",
                                                "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                                "text": "In the ADF, while the numbers vary between the individual services and the reserves, employment is no comfortable sinecure for any personnel and thus does not appeal to many people, male or female, especially under current pay scales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1a85cd9-2713-4ad1-be6e-e2233d346c7d",
                                                "sense_id": "199f905d-1a3d-382e-974e-758fb84a8ed6",
                                                "text": "However, by the time of World War II (if not before), politics, at least in the federal sphere, was no longer regarded as sinecure for well-intentioned part-timers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff60e789-baad-39ca-ad02-00ba0bff349a",
                                        "entry_id": "5f03727e-c911-33ca-9e75-1fbc2979df72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ecclesiastical benefice without the care of souls."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sinecure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7f16168-4185-33df-b099-8339facf9e46",
                                        "entry_id": "a55a31c0-9fe8-306e-ad3a-393e8f4329a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Requiring no work for an ample reward."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9618f7d9-0999-4945-ae3d-71f425a9a986",
                                                "sense_id": "e7f16168-4185-33df-b099-8339facf9e46",
                                                "text": "By the act of union (1800), the offices of Irish secretary, a sinecure post, and lord lieutenant's secretary were combined."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd8265ae-75dc-3c59-ad03-b31a47fd6a8f",
                                        "entry_id": "a55a31c0-9fe8-306e-ad3a-393e8f4329a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the appearance of functionality without being of any actual use or purpose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04d5c355-616a-4365-a7ec-6f599325d791",
                                                "sense_id": "dd8265ae-75dc-3c59-ad03-b31a47fd6a8f",
                                                "text": "The old man hastily pulled down his spectacles from their sinecure office on his forehead, and looked at her with an expression of most angry amazement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sinecure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "256623d2-f511-3884-8c7e-77bee4b58e5d",
                                        "entry_id": "d9c2ca1f-b875-3247-9940-974b88af265f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put or place in a sinecure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "35168f34-dbb4-4927-831d-60c42246e766",
                        "source_entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sinekure",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sinekure",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd68511e-8e1b-38f4-90c9-6960a243af9d",
                                        "entry_id": "a38827bc-f0b5-3306-b87e-a82d7938986b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "einträgliche Position ohne Dienstaufgaben"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fef76ab6-7d78-4b21-802c-bdfba3a99048",
                                                "sense_id": "dd68511e-8e1b-38f4-90c9-6960a243af9d",
                                                "text": "„Dann folgt seine Exzellenz der Königliche Kämmerer - ohne Sinekure, denn Seine Majestät pflegen sich eigenhändig anzukleiden, außer beim Landurlaub in Waikiki, denn dort braucht der König überhaupt keine Kleider.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a30b90-056e-4cd2-96fa-6a6db2558236",
                                                "sense_id": "dd68511e-8e1b-38f4-90c9-6960a243af9d",
                                                "text": "„Bisher war es eine Sinekure gewesen: das bislang schwierigste medizinische Problem, das ihm begegnet war, hatte so weit jenseits der von ihm zu erwartenden Kenntnisse gelegen, dass er es mit gutem Gewissen ablehnen konnte.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5a3b558-2284-4b99-8bb8-a12f4050ef9d",
                                                "sense_id": "dd68511e-8e1b-38f4-90c9-6960a243af9d",
                                                "text": "„Im August 1775, wenige Wochen nach der Rückkehr von seiner zweiten Pazifikreise, beantragte er eine Sinekure als Kapitän im Königlichen Hospital in Greenwich, das medizinische Einrichtung und Heim für ältere Seeleute zugleich war.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6e6bff1-b7d2-4253-bd2a-f535b852c9de",
                                                "sense_id": "dd68511e-8e1b-38f4-90c9-6960a243af9d",
                                                "text": "„Sie kannte und verachtete auch die satten Gläubigen, die aus seinem Leiden eine fette Sinekure machten.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "788957ee-93fe-47bf-b82a-a27d65bbe1f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "f567b2c3-db19-34c4-9078-3fbb635f9946",
                        "target_lang_word": "sinécure",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sinécure",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "666643f8-9ae1-30ee-b7ea-072ceee99554",
                                        "entry_id": "80a9ba42-21f5-34e2-ad9a-d1d4cd9a77c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Place ou titre qui produit des émoluments et qui n’oblige à aucun travail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a180b5da-1488-4419-a17e-cb373eaf0642",
                                                "sense_id": "666643f8-9ae1-30ee-b7ea-072ceee99554",
                                                "text": "Rien de plus difficile à déloger d’une sinécure, que des fainéants sans valeur personnelle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b8e6196-850d-4fd3-889c-b543a09c337f",
                                                "sense_id": "666643f8-9ae1-30ee-b7ea-072ceee99554",
                                                "text": "J’ai de traitement, de mes sinécures, de l’Académie et de mon libraire, environ trente mille francs par an, fortune énorme pour un garçon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66efbd51-47ad-40a4-998c-f0f921e6df06",
                                                "sense_id": "666643f8-9ae1-30ee-b7ea-072ceee99554",
                                                "text": "C’est une fonction peu laborieuse en temps de paix, puisqu’il ne reste alors de la milice que les cadres et les états-majors, conservés comme une source de sinécures pour l’aristocratie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c05f5b2-2e21-42a6-af36-b3f7f0b24010",
                                                "sense_id": "666643f8-9ae1-30ee-b7ea-072ceee99554",
                                                "text": "[…] d’écœurants petits snobs, riches pour la plupart, en tout cas oisifs, ou lotis de quelque sinécure dans quelque ministère — ce qui est tout comme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee91eb52-b6ba-4e57-858d-ea86a90d3cb3",
                                                "sense_id": "666643f8-9ae1-30ee-b7ea-072ceee99554",
                                                "text": "Arsène ne tarda pas à s’apercevoir que son poste de secrétaire ressemblait furieusement à une sinécure. En deux mois, il n’eut que quatre lettres insignifiantes à recopier et ne fut appelé qu’une fois dans le bureau de son patron, ce qui ne lui permit qu’une fois de contempler officiellement le coffre-fort."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d389e507-6c7f-327c-b624-0dbd9dfeea7f",
                                        "entry_id": "80a9ba42-21f5-34e2-ad9a-d1d4cd9a77c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Emploi fortement rémunéré pour très peu de travail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67487865-75c9-3ab5-9313-a86dad9b27f7",
                                        "entry_id": "80a9ba42-21f5-34e2-ad9a-d1d4cd9a77c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chose ou expérience agréable et/ou ne demandant pas d'effort. Note d’usage : utilisé dans une forme négative pour indiquer que c’est désagréable ou demande de grands efforts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f78fb608-5fe2-4a4d-b76f-8a4eaf6b05d0",
                                                "sense_id": "67487865-75c9-3ab5-9313-a86dad9b27f7",
                                                "text": "La grossesse n’avait pas été une sinécure et, maintenant qu’Agnès entamait les dernières semaines, c’était pire que tout."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "015e1989-9096-4000-8ec2-759d8a765eea",
                                                "sense_id": "67487865-75c9-3ab5-9313-a86dad9b27f7",
                                                "text": "Eh ben allez, une journée de plus en moins, on va aller dormir et puis demain on recommence. J'peux vous dire que tavernier, c'est pas une sinécure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
